# mutgap_mem_tracker_compact_stale_span: Compaction leaves the last block's span right. A task of 16 x 4096 pages, every leaf one RAM page, and 30,720 one-page runs at every other page fill 128 blocks of 240 (as newops_range_tracker_limit). 200 runs unmapped in each of blocks 10 and 11; a map into a gap near the end of block 127 finds 128 blocks and compacts: block 10 takes block 11's 40 runs and it is removed, and every later block takes 160 runs from the next, whose span is set to its remaining runs; the last, block 126 now, keeps 80 runs and the span of just those, [61280, 61439), and the map adds a run to it. 159 one-page runs after it, from page 61440, fill it to 240 and its span to [61280, 61757). A run at page 61758 is past it (Less), and with 127 blocks it opens block 127. A map into a gap in the first half of block 126 (page 61281) then finds it full and 128 blocks, compacts, which frees nothing, and faults "Range too complex" after the host mapped the page. Blocks only; block calls as counts and a digest.
